{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# LangGraph \u2014 State Machines for Agents Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: state and nodes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from typing import Annotated, TypedDict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from langchain_core.messages import AnyMessage, HumanMessage, AIMessage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from langgraph.graph import StateGraph, END"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from langgraph.graph.message import add_messages"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from langgraph.prebuilt import ToolNode"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from langgraph.checkpoint.memory import MemorySaver"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class State(TypedDict):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    messages: Annotated[list[AnyMessage], add_messages]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def agent_node(state: State) -> dict:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    response = llm.invoke(state[\"messages\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return {\"messages\": [response]}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def should_continue(state: State) -> str:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    last = state[\"messages\"][-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return \"tools\" if getattr(last, \"tool_calls\", None) else END"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tool_node = ToolNode(tools=[search_web, read_file])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "graph = StateGraph(State)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "graph.add_node(\"agent\", agent_node)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "graph.add_node(\"tools\", tool_node)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "graph.set_entry_point(\"agent\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "graph.add_conditional_edges(\"agent\", should_continue, {\"tools\": \"tools\", END: END})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "graph.add_edge(\"tools\", \"agent\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "app = graph.compile(checkpointer=MemorySaver())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`add_messages` is the reducer that makes the message list accumulate instead of overwrite. Forgetting it is the most common LangGraph bug."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: run with a thread"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "config = {\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"user-42\"}}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for event in app.stream("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {\"messages\": [HumanMessage(\"find the Anthropic headquarters address\")]},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    config,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    stream_mode=\"updates\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(event)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Every update is a dict `{node_name: state_delta}`. Your frontend can stream these to the UI so users see \"agent is thinking\u2026 calling search_web\u2026 got result\u2026 answering.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: add a human-in-the-loop interrupt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Mark a node so execution pauses before it runs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "app = graph.compile("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    checkpointer=MemorySaver(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    interrupt_before=[\"tools\"],  # pause before every tool call"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "state = app.invoke({\"messages\": [HumanMessage(\"delete the production database\")]}, config)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# state[\"__interrupt__\"] is set. Inspect proposed tool calls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# If approved:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from langgraph.types import Command"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "app.invoke(Command(resume=True), config)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# If denied: write a rejection message and resume"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "app.update_state(config, {\"messages\": [AIMessage(\"Blocked by human reviewer.\")]})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The state, the checkpoint, and the thread all persist across the interrupt. Nothing is in memory except during execution."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: time-travel for debugging"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "history = list(app.get_state_history(config))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for snapshot in history:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(snapshot.values[\"messages\"][-1].content[:80], snapshot.config)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Fork from a prior checkpoint"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "target = history[3].config  # three steps back"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for event in app.stream(None, target, stream_mode=\"values\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pass  # replay from that point forward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Passing `None` as the input replays from the given checkpoint; passing a value appends it as an update to that checkpoint's state before resuming. This is how you reproduce a bad agent run without re-running the whole conversation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: swap the checkpointer for production"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from langgraph.checkpoint.postgres import PostgresSaver"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "with PostgresSaver.from_conn_string(\"postgresql://...\") as checkpointer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    checkpointer.setup()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    app = graph.compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "SQLite, Redis, and Postgres are shipped. `MemorySaver` is for tests. Anything that persists across restarts wants a real store."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    }
  ],
